<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA GETS GOOD 1997 BARLEY CROP.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA GETS GOOD 1997 BARLEY CROP.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania has brought in 1.46 million tonnes of barley with the harvest all but complete, exceeding for previous forecasts and last year's figures, the agriculture ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ministry data said harvesting had been completed on 98 percent of the land sown to barley, or 410,862 hectares. Earlier forecasts had put the 1997 barley crop at 1.36 million tonnes and last year's harvest stood at 980,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;The remaining two percent will he harvested within the next two or three days, weather permitting,&quot; a ministry official said.</p>
<p>Average yield per hectare was 3,591 kg, higher than the ministry's initial estimates of 3,278, data also showed.</p>
<p>-- Adrian Dascalu, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
